fully wireless earbuds are quickly  becoming the new standard for listening  to music or basically anything else  now that we're getting into 2021 and  beyond  so in this video we're gonna compare the  three  best pairs of fully wireless earbuds to  see which ones are the best for each use  case we've got apple's incredibly  popular airpods pro for 250  or actually on sale right now on amazon  for 197  we've got sony's brand new wf  wf-1000xm4s that are known for having  the best noise cancellation  which are priced at a pretty high 278  dollars  and we've got samsung's new galaxy buds  pro  for 200 or currently on sale for only  170 on amazon  less expensive than the other two so  without further ado let's get right into  comparing these earbuds in a bunch of  different categories  starting with the size and the  portability of the cases  the case on the galaxy buds pro is  actually the smallest in terms of the  footprint  but it's a lot thicker than the airpods  pro and surprisingly  the sony's are not only the largest but  also the  thickest as well but it is a huge  improvement  over last year's xm3s in terms of the  weight of the cases themselves  the airpods case is actually the  heaviest  compared to the surprisingly light sony  case now for design  and build quality because the sony's are  so lightweight  the case feels a little bit cheap  because of the matte plastic feel  that doesn't seem as solid now the  galaxy buds are a small step  up and the airpods pro case does seem to  have the best build quality  and design now in terms of the quality  of the hinges the airpods pro case has a  very solid  metal hinge that feels very nice to  flick open  with a pretty strong magnet holding the  case closed  and unfortunately the sony's have the  weakest magnet and therefore have the  highest chance  of opening if it falls on top of that  both the galaxy buds pro and the sonys  have plastic hinges that don't feel as  nice and cause the top of the cases  to wiggle especially on the sony's  now in terms of how much battery life is  packed into the cases themselves  excluding the earbuds the airpods pro  case holds enough power to give you  19 more hours of listening time with  noise cancellation on  while the sony's give you 16 more hours  and the galaxy buttons pro give you an  extra 13 hours  and what's great this year is that all  of these earbuds support wireless  charging  whereas in last year's comparison only  the airpods pro had it however the  airpods pro case uses  lightning to charge which is a bit  disappointing  compared to usbc on the other two now  opening up the cases both  the airpods pro and the sony's feel very  satisfying when you're taking them out  and putting them back into the case with  a very strong magnetic feel  but on the galaxy but pro the magnetic  connection is  very weak so it takes very little effort  to take them out  and that causes them to fall out very  easily  compared to the other two that fit very  snugly now before we get into comparing  the audio quality between these wireless  earbuds  let's compare some of the fine details  of the earbuds themselves  the airpods pro have a very sleek low  profile shape  with a short stem sticking out for  better microphone quality  and because of the stem the airpods look  quite a bit smaller than the other two  especially the very large and bulbous  sonys now in terms of the weight of the  earbuds themselves  the airpods pro are by far the lightest  with the sony's being the heaviest  as expected due to the size and that's  probably why they also get the best  battery life by far eight hours per bud  with anc on  compared to just 4.5 hours on the  airpods pro  and five hours with the galaxy butts pro  in terms of the design  they honestly look really nice and clean  but i don't really like the  chrome-like reflective finish on the  galaxy but pro  which can gather fingerprints or smudges  the airpods pro look very classy and  simple  with the glossy white plastic design but  the sony's  i would say look by far the most premium  or professional  with a nice matte finish and clean  design elements  now in terms of comfort in the ears the  airpods pro are by far the most  comfortable out of the three  and there's two very good reasons for it  while both the sony's and galaxy buds  pro have a hard plastic tube  that enters your ear canal with the  sony's tube  being quite a bit longer the earpods pro  actually have a completely flush speaker  grill  so the only thing that goes into your  ear canal is the very soft  silicone ear tip and the sony's actually  come with foam ear tips  that you have to squish like earplugs  each  and every time you want to put them in  your ears which i've got to say is  extremely annoying because i found  myself  taking them out multiple times to squish  them down even further  compared to the other earbuds that  simply pop right in  on top of that all of these earbuds  create a seal inside of your ears for  better bass  sound quality and noise cancellation but  the earpods pro  actually have a vent that releases the  air pressure within your  ear and while the galaxy buds pro say  they have a vent and they do  it doesn't really seem to do that much  and the sony's don't really offer  anything like that at all  so your ears end up feeling the most  plugged now on top of that because of  the very large size of the sony xm4s it  kind of puts  pressure on your ears combined with the  expanding foam  that also puts a bit of pressure on the  inside of your ear canals  so overall the airpods pro feel  absolutely the most comfortable thanks  to the softer ear tip design the venting  feature  and the lighter weight now getting into  sound quality  the galaxy buds pro are the only ones  that actually come with two speakers in  each earbud  a woofer and a tweeter and because of  that they have a ton of bass  while also having very bright highs due  to the tweeters  but unfortunately they are really  lacking in the mids  which leads to vocals not really  sounding natural at all  and overall not as well balanced sound  now for the airpods pro  they do very well in terms of the mids  with vocal sounding super clean  full and natural the bass definitely  isn't as heavy as the buds pro  but it's very tight and accurate and  overall the airpods pro are actually  louder  than the butts pro which makes them even  more impressive and now  for the sonys they absolutely killed it  in my opinion  now the volume definitely isn't as loud  as the earpods pro  especially in the high notes which i do  miss  but the overall sound quality is  incredible vocals sound perfect  being natural just like on the airpods  pro but with the sonys  there seems to be the most separation  between sound frequencies  so it sounds very clean whereas with the  airpods pro  some of the frequencies kind of clash  together just a little bit  and i've got to say that the sound stage  feels the widest on the sony's as well  and out of all of these earbuds the  sonys give you bass  that's very deep loud punchy and  accurate  all at the same time so overall they're  very well balanced compared to the  airpods pro  that seem to be heavy on the high notes  and the galaxy buds pro that are greatly  lacking  in terms of the mids so yeah the sony's  definitely have the best sound quality  now in terms of noise cancellation  the galaxy butts pro are by far the  worst with the airpods pro being a nice  step  up and the sony's completely destroying  the other two  getting rid of more noise but in terms  of the ambient or transparency modes  the airpods pro absolutely kill it here  with everything like vocals and noises  sounding almost exactly like it does  without having anything at all in your  ears  which is extremely impressive now with  the galaxy buds and the sonys  the ambient modes don't work nearly as  well making your voice sound a bit  muted and other people's voices don't  sound very natural at all  like they do with the airpods pro now  before we get into which buds we  recommend  i want to go through a couple of the  feature and software differences  the galaxy buds pro have ipx 7 water  resistance  much better than ipx4 on the other two  and out of all of them  the airpods pro were also the most  reliable  basically always staying connected to my  iphone while the other two would  occasionally disconnect out of nowhere  for a split second the sony's actually  require you to download their headphone  connect app  to use the earbuds but it crashed on me  a few times  and the initial software update took  forever  over 30 minutes which was very annoying  but the beauty about the airpods pro is  that they don't require anything at all  no apps no software updates they just  connect  instantly if you have an iphone so you  don't even have to go into the bluetooth  menu  and on top of that they automatically  sync to the rest of your apple devices  that are logged into your apple id  which is super convenient for apple  users and on top of that  i prefer these stem controls much better  than the touch controls on the others  because touch can be kind of unreliable  at times and when you for example  double tap on them to skip tracks they  kind of push the earbuds further into  your ears  which can get very annoying especially  since the sony's kind of hurt your ears  after a while  compared to the airpods where you simply  squeeze the stem  and now finally let's get into which  earbuds we recommend for each use case  the galaxy butts pro are definitely the  least expensive  sitting at 170 on sale right now or 200  retail but they just don't sound nearly  as good  as either the airpod pros or the sony's  and on top of that the noise  cancellation and ambient noise features  were by far  the worst out of the bunch but due to  the compact design of the earbuds  and the ipx7 water resistance they could  be great for someone who likes to work  out  or maybe even swim the sony's definitely  have the best sound quality  and the best noise cancellation but  you're gonna be paying 278 dollars for  them  and they also aren't nearly as  comfortable as the airpods pro  yes the earbuds themselves do have the  best battery life but your ears honestly  start hurting after a while  because of the very large size that sort  of squeezes into your ear  and the foam tips that expand putting  pressure on your ear canals  but with the airpods pro the tubeless  soft  ear tip design is incredible for comfort  along with the venting feature  that gets rid of pressure in your ears  and the lightweight design  that lets you listen to them for hours  and the airpods pro  are by far the most reliable because  they basically never glitch out or  disconnect  like the other sometimes do they don't  require any setup or software updates or  downloads  and they fit perfectly into the apple  ecosystem  for iphone users they just work right  out of the box  and they work very well but if you're  all about having the absolute  best sound quality or the best active  noise cancellation  then i would say that spending the extra  cash on the sony's  is definitely worth the price especially  if you're an android user  but if you're okay with sacrificing some  of the sound quality and anc  performance to get absolutely incredible  comfort  convenience reliability better  transparency mode and a much lower 200  price tag on amazon right now then i  would honestly just go for the airpods  pro and as long as the airpods pro are  on sale  i honestly wouldn't recommend the galaxy  but pro  because you have to compromise in so  many different areas  so there you guys have it hopefully this  video helped you make a decision  and if it did feel free to use our links  down below to the best deals on these  earbuds  and if you enjoyed the video go ahead  and click the circle about to subscribe  for more videos like this one  definitely check out one of these two  right 